Riptide @VERSION@ - TCP/IP stack for AmigaOS 3.x (68020 or better)
==================================================================

Installing
----------

Double-click "Install_Riptide" (it uses the standard Amiga Installer,
Installer 43.x or InstallerLG). From a Shell:

  cd Riptide
  Installer Install_Riptide

The installer

  * copies Riptide, rtcheck and the network tools (ip, ifconfig, route,
    arp, netstat, ping, traceroute, host, sysctl, hostname, nc, ftp) to
    C: (Expert users can pick another drawer),
  * installs the documentation in <Work: or SYS:>Riptide/Docs and,
    if you ask for it, the SDK in <Work: or SYS:>Riptide/SDK,
  * writes ENVARC:Riptide/riptide.conf (and copies it to ENV:Riptide/)
    for the emulator's uaenet.device with DHCP, or for another SANA-II
    device and a static address,
  * adds a ";BEGIN Riptide" block to S:User-Startup that starts Riptide
    at boot, and can start it right away.

It warns about another running TCP/IP stack or the emulator's
bsdsocket.library emulation, and offers to rename another stack's
LIBS:bsdsocket.library to bsdsocket.library.disabled. Run it again to
update or to uninstall.

Emulators
---------

FS-UAE:  uae_sana2 = 1
         network_card = a2065
WinUAE:  enable uaenet.device; turn off bsdsocket.library emulation.

With the emulator's slirp network Riptide gets 10.0.2.15 by DHCP; the
host is 10.0.2.2 and the DNS forwarder 10.0.2.3.

Testing
-------

  Riptide STATUS
  rtcheck -v
  ping -c 3 10.0.2.2

Manual installation
-------------------

  1. Copy C/#? to C:.
  2. Put a configuration in ENVARC:Riptide/riptide.conf and
     ENV:Riptide/riptide.conf (Docs/riptide-uaenet.conf is an example).
  3. Start it with "Run >NIL: Riptide", e.g. from S:User-Startup.

